                <div><span>Services & infrastructure</span><p>JSON · AWS · Heroku · Azure APIs · Docker</p></div>
                <div><span>Product & tools</span><p>Figma · Git · GitHub · GitLab</p></div>
              </div>
            </section>
            <p class="no-bg experience-detail-section">
              <!------------------- DRIME PLAYER  ----------------->
              <span class="experience-section-kicker">01 · Case study</span>
              <span class="experience-section-title">DRIME Player & .drime file format</span></br></br>
                For professionals/clients</br><br>
                - Video tutorials are filmed by the DRIME team and optimized for all screen resolutions.<br>
                - Features include multi-language broadcasting via voiceovers, subtitles, and dynamic designs in all selected languages, plus voice commands. Tutorials/manuals can be broken into step-by-step sequences.<br>
                - Beyond the DRIME platform’s video library, clients can embed single videos or entire libraries on their own sites via iframes (indexed by Google).<br>
                - The platform includes a dashboard with “Smart Indicators”, user-rights management, custom iframes, and QR codes. Dynamic video designs were also road-mapped.</br><br>
                For end users</br><br>
                - A video playback experience that adapts to screen resolution, with step-by-step or continuous playback, voice commands, sound/subtitle settings, and language selection.<br>
                - By default, the video displays in the user’s browser language when available, otherwise in English.<br>
            </p>
            <!------------------- KEY ACHIEVEMENTS  ----------------->
             <p><span class="bold">Key Achievements — Player</span></br></br>
              - Developed new features end to end (front end & back end).</br>
              - Player redesign: persistent sound/subtitle settings; CSS & Lottie animations for buttons; step counters for step-by-step videos; improved voice commands.</br>
              - Homepage redesign with Lottie animations and menu creation.</br>
              - Fixed video creation crashes (>5 videos) by implementing a background job for multilingual generation; later redesigned the pipeline for scalability.</br>
